    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Mughal Empire was founded by the Timurid prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#babur">Babur</a> in 1526 and came to rule most of the Indian subcontinent.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#akbar">Akbar</a>'s cash revenue system, ranked nobility and religious accommodation built one of the largest economies of its age.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>'s costly wars, regional revolts and the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#east-india-company">East India Company</a> hollowed it out before its end in 1858.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#babur">Babur</a> descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#timur">Timur</a> on his father's side and from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> on his mother's, and his dynasty's name comes from the Persian word for Mongol.</p></aside>
    </section>

